/T (Manual irrigation depends on a person observing plants and deciding when to water them. Timer-based irrigation can also water plants at fixed times even when the soil condition does not require it. The project addresses this basic problem by demonstrating a controller that makes an irrigation decision from a soil-condition value.)
/E (Manual irrigation depends on a person observing plants and deciding when to water them. Timer-based irrigation can also water plants at fixed times even when the soil condition does not require it. The project addresses this basic problem by demonstrating a controller that makes an irrigation decision from a soil-condition value.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 65 0 R
/T (The target behavior is simple: when the soil is considered dry, the irrigation output should turn ON; when the soil is considered wet, the output should turn OFF. The system should also provide a visible status so that the user can understand the current value and pump state.)
/E (The target behavior is simple: when the soil is considered dry, the irrigation output should turn ON; when the soil is considered wet, the output should turn OFF. The system should also provide a visible status so that the user can understand the current value and pump state.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
