/T (For this simulation, the main constraints considered were decision correctness, update interval, display behavior, repeatability and the limits of simulation. The code updates the simulated value once per second because the loop ends with a one-second delay. The threshold logic is deterministic, so the same value should always produce the same relay decision.)
/E (For this simulation, the main constraints considered were decision correctness, update interval, display behavior, repeatability and the limits of simulation. The code updates the simulated value once per second because the loop ends with a one-second delay. The threshold logic is deterministic, so the same value should always produce the same relay decision.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
