690 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Smart Irrigation System demonstrates a complete embedded control concept using ESP32, threshold-based decision making, relay control and OLED feedback. The Wokwi simulation provides a repeatable environment for observing dry and wet operating states.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 661 0 R
/Next 701 0 R
>>
endobj
691 0 obj
<<
/Title (The most important limitation is that the present program simulates the soil value instead of reading the potentiometer/physical sensor. The next development step is therefore to connect the actual input to the control algorithm and then validate the complete system with a real pump and safe power-control hardware.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 661 0 R
/Prev 701 0 R
>>
endobj
692 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project work involved understanding the circuit, preparing the ESP32 program, interfacing the OLED through I2C, implementing threshold logic, observing serial output, testing dry and wet conditions and documenting the result. The Wokwi environment made it possible to repeat the tests safely without using a physical pump.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 613 0 R
/Prev 684 0 R
/Next 702 0 R
>>
endobj
